===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[cluster]] of [[heterogeneous]] [[thing]]s.
#* {{quote-book|author=Richard Chenevix Trench|authorlink=Richard Chenevix Trench|chapter=The Evangelical, Compared with Other Cycles of Miracles|title=Notes on the Miracles of Our Lord|location=London|publisher=[[w:John William Parker|John W[illiam] Parker]],{{nb...|West Strand}}|year=1846|section=section 2 (The Miracles of the Apocryphal Gospels)|page=39|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=pPVhAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA39|oclc=40921107|passage=They [miracles in the canonical gospels] are held, too, together by his [Jesus Christ's] strong and central personality, which does not leave them a '''conglomerate''' of marvellous anecdotes accidentally heaped together, but parts of a great organic whole, of which every part is in vital coherence with every other.}}
# {{lb|en|business}} A [[corporation]] [[form#Verb|formed]] by the [[combination]] of several [[small]]er corporations whose activities are [[unrelated]] to the corporation's [[primary]] [[activity]].
#* {{quote-web|title=ESAs [European Supervisory Authorities] Publish the List of Financial Conglomerates|url=https://www.eba.europa.eu/-/esas-publish-the-list-of-financial-conglomerates|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20180724151321/https://www.eba.europa.eu/-/esas-publish-the-list-of-financial-conglomerates|archivedate=24 July 2018|work={{w|European Banking Authority}}|date=5 December 2017|passage=The 2017 list includes 80 financial '''conglomerates''' with the head of group located in the European Union or European Economic Area, one financial '''conglomerate''' with the head of group in Switzerland, one in Bermuda, and two in the United States.}}
# {{lb|en|geology}} A [[rock#Noun|rock]] consisting of [[gravel]] or [[pebble]]s [[embed#Verb|embedded]] in a [[matrix]].
#* {{quote-book|author=Charles Lyell|authorlink=Charles Lyell|chapter=Aqueous Rocks—Their Composition and Forms of Stratification|title=Elements of Geology|location=London|publisher=[[w:John Murray (publisher)|John Murray]],{{nb...|Albemarle Street}}|year=1838|page=27|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=PFsOAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA27|oclc=31070870|passage=When sandstone is coarse-grained, it is usually called ''grit''. If the grains are rounded, and large enough to be called pebbles, it becomes a '''''conglomerate''''', or ''pudding-stone'', which may consist of pieces of one or of many different kinds of rock. A '''conglomerate''', therefore, is simply gravel bound together by a cement.}}
#* {{RQ:Hugo Man Who Laughs|volume=I|part=I|book=III|chapter=Chesil|page=156|passage=Calcareous lias, slate, and trap are still to be found there, rising from layers of '''conglomerate''' like teeth out of a gum. But the pickaxe has broken up and levelled those bristling, rugged peaks which were once the homes of the eagles.}}
#* {{quote-book|author=Fitz Hugh Ludlow|authorlink=Fitz Hugh Ludlow|chapter=Comstock’s.—A Buffalo Hunt.|title=The Heart of the Continent: A Record of Travel across the Plains and in Oregon,{{nb...|with an Examination of the Mormon Principle}}|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Published by [[w:Henry Oscar Houghton|Hurd and Houghton]];{{nb...|Cambridge, Mass.: Riverside Press}}|year=1870|page=97|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=PN9CAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA97|oclc=27675147|passage=Everywhere in the river appeared a very remarkable '''conglomerate''', and like the slate in exhibiting all the stages of formation. The matrix was the blue clay of the bank, the rubble was the gravel of the bottom.}}
#* {{quote-book|author=J. B. Wright|author2=D. A. Hastings|author3= W. B Jones|author4=H. R. Williams|chapter=The Pan African of West Africa – the Eastern Domain|title=Geology and Mineral Resources of West Africa|location=London|publisher=[[w:Allen & Unwin|George Allen & Unwin (Publishers)]]|year=1985|section=part I (The Precambrian of West Africa)|page=59|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=qiAyBwAAQBAJ&pg=PA59|column=1|doi=10.1007/978-94-015-3932-6|isbn=978-94-015-3934-0|passage=The Middle Voltaian lies unconformably on the Lower Voltaian with a basal '''conglomerate''' that can be correlated with '''conglomerates''' of the Buem Formation. Both sets of '''conglomerates''' have been interpreted as tillites, possibly equivalent to the Infracambrian tillites of the Rokelide–Mauritanide belt west of the craton {{...}} and in the Taoudeni Basin{{nb...}}.}}

