===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[cluster#Verb|Clustered]] together into a [[mass#Noun|mass]].
#: {{ux|en|'''conglomerate''' flowers}}
#* {{RQ:Bacon Sylva Sylvarum|century=III|chapter=Consent of Visibles, and Audibles|page=69|para=267|passage=The ''Beames of Light'', when they are ''multiplied'' and '''''conglomerate''''', generate ''Heat''; which is a different Action, from the Action of ''Sight'': {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|author=George Cheyne|authorlink=George Cheyne (physician)|chapter=Of the Existence of a Deity|title=Philosophical Principles of Natural Religion:{{nb...|Containing the Elements of Natural Philosophy, and the Proofs for Natural Religion, Arising from Them.}}|location=London|publisher=Printed for George Strahan{{nb...|at the Golden Bull in Cornhill over against the Royal Exchange}}|year=1705|section=§&nbsp;XXXV|page=213|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/philosophicalpri00cheyuoft#page/213/mode/1up|oclc=12981367|passage=By the motion of the ''Heart'', through the ''Emulgent'' Branches, the Blood is brought to the ''Kidneys'', and is there freed of its ''Serum'' by their little ''Glands'', {{...}} Much after the ſame manner, are their proper Fluids ſeparated from the Blood in the ''Liver'', ''Sweetbread'', ''Teſticles'', and the other ''Conglobat'' and '''''Conglomerate''' Glands'' of the Body{{nb...}}.}}
# {{lb|en|geology}} [[compose|Composed]] of [[fragment#Noun|fragments]] of [[rock#Noun|rock]], [[pebble]]s, or [[stone#Noun|stones]] [[cement#Verb|cemented]] together.
#* {{quote-book|author=Robert T. Ryder|author2=Alan Thomson|chapter=Abstract|title=Tectonically Controlled Fan Delta and Submarine Fan Sedimentation of Late Miocene Age, Southern Temblor Range, California|series=[[w:United States Geological Survey|U.S. Geological Survey]] Professional Paper|seriesvolume=1442|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=[[w:United States Government Publishing Office|United States Government Printing Office]]|year=1989|page=1|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=8VvwAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA1|oclc=644957658|passage=The Santa Margarita Formation in the southern Temblor Range, composed of '''conglomerate''' and subordinate sandstone, evolved as a large complex of fan deltas and submarine fans in late Miocene time.}}
#* {{quote-book|author=Megh Raj Dhital|chapter=Siwaliks of Arun–Tamar Region|title=Geology of the Nepal Himalaya: Regional Perspective of the Classic Collided Orogen|series=Regional Geology Reviews|location=Cham, Switzerland; Heidelberg|publisher=[[w:Springer Nature|Springer International Publishing]]|year=2015|section=section 33.2 (Siwaliks)|page=433|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=2OybBgAAQBAJ&pg=PA433|column=2|doi=10.1007/978-3-319-02496-7_33|isbn=978-3-319-02495-0|passage=He also documented some intercalated mottled reddish clays and marls, and the upper horizons containing bluish clays with '''conglomerate''' beds.}}

