===Verb===
{{en-verb|conglomerat}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[combine#Verb|combine]] together into a [[large]]r [[mass#Noun|mass]].
#* {{quote-book|author=“an artilleryman” [pseudonym]|title=A Popular Introduction to Rifled Ordnance, for the Use of Learners of the Art of Gunnery|location=Woolwich, London|publisher=Boddy and Co., military printers,{{nb...|Artillery Place.}}|year=1871|pages=50–51|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=LE4BAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA51|oclc=556982036|passage=The tin cyliner, filled with iron balls, which is fired from our smooth-bored guns, was unsuitable for a rifled gun, because the breaking up of such a projectile in the bore was likely to injure the rifling. Then again, lead balls could not well be substituted for iron ones on account of their liability to '''conglomerate''' or adhere together in lumps.}}
#* {{quote-book|author=Richard J. Hand|author2=Andrew Purssel|chapter=Introduction|title=Adapting {{w|Graham Greene}}|location=London; New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Palgrave Macmillan|Palgrave]]|year=2015|page=1|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=kKC7BgAAQBAJ&pg=PA1|isbn=978-0-230-57904-0|passage=Looked at from this angle, we soon realize that the perceived greatness of [[w:William Shakespeare|[William] Shakespeare]] lies less in his 'originality', than in his exceptional ability to '''conglomerate''' and re-apply materials and models in the creation of new dramatic works.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|business}} To combine together into a larger [[corporation]].

